    "q-221380": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221380",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $14∣p$ then $7∣p$\n\nII. If $14∣p$ then $4∣p$\n\nIII. If $21∣p$ then $3∣p$",
      "worked_solution": "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $7∣14.$ Therefore, we have\n$7∣14$ and $14∣p,$ which implies that $7∣p.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $p=14.$ Then, $14∣14$ but $4∤14.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $3∣21.$ Therefore, we have\n$3∣21$ and $21∣p,$ which implies that $3∣p.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
