    "q-221377": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221377",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $16∣n$ then $8∣n$\n\nII. If $16∣n$ then $12∣n$\n\nIII. If $4∣n$ then $16∣n$",
      "worked_solution": "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $8∣16.$ Therefore, we have\n$8∣16$ and $16∣n,$ which implies that $8∣n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $n=16.$ Then, $16∣16$ but $12∤16.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $n=4.$ Then, $4∣4$ but $16∤4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
