    "q-93660": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93660",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $3\\,|\\,a$ and $8\\,|\\,a$ then $24\\,|\\,a$\n\nII. If $10\\,|\\,b$ and $21\\,|\\,b$ then $210\\,|\\,b$\n\nIII. If ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,c$ and ${4}^{2}\\,|\\,c$ then $144\\,|\\,c$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(3,8)=1$ and $3\\cdot 8=24.$ Therefore, we have $(3\\,|\\,a),(8\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(3,8)=1,$ which implies $(24\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1$ and $10\\cdot 21=210.$ Therefore, we have $(10\\,|\\,b),(21\\,|\\,b),$ and $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1,$ which implies $(210\\,|\\,b).$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},{4}^{2})=1$ and ${3}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{2}=144.$ Therefore, we have $({3}^{2}\\,|\\,c),({4}^{2}\\,|\\,c),$ and $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},{4}^{2})=1,$ which implies $(144\\,|\\,c).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
